A friend and I went in on a computer together - a VAX server.  He is
doing all the work to set it up and to save him some time I have been
trying to find documentation on how to start out using VMS.  I need to
learn how to program and write @command files, and how to perform sysop
tasks.  I will be getting a sysop account on it since I helped pay for
it.  So, it makes sense that I know how to be a sysop doesn't it :-)  I
just need sources of information that someone who has never used VMS
before can understand that describe the commands and syntax in simple
form.

BTW, this friend will be making this server machine public.  I have
heard that a free public vax server is unheard of - and we will be
offering free accounts on a VMS server, probably with 2000 blacks to
start out with.  You will be able to program and compile etc.....  there
is a BBS system that my friend has written with an interactive chat,
menu for novice users (like myself :-), and other features as well as a
playable MUD (eventually...... its still being programmed).  The server
is physically here and being set up at the current moment, not available
yet to the public.  I can't even log into it yet and I paid for part of
it :-)  If interested, call my answering service at (877) 860-0396.  You
may leave a fax at the same number if you wish.  Leave your email
address there or other means of contacting you.  I will contact you when
the server is ready to log into.  Please direct any replies to this post
to hobootis@ureach.com AND this newsgroup.  I will check my mailbox more
often than this newgroup, so I will get your messages sooner if you
email me directly.  SPAM WILL NOT BE TOLERATED.

